{:edb/db-before-t 1578 :edb/db-after-t 1579 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534891 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:31:00.585Z" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186193324 1068 #edb/ref 17592186191871 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186193324 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186193324 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186193324 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fc71859cb4d1e58ea3d15c2da66bce014898281fe237f2e0c2396f96c84c9e79.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ef/eff037b96b6a42120fdfa112a98d1e0749cdd56bd89acd647db448b08d7323ad.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-1<y<0\\,\\}.\n$$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186193324 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fc71859cb4d1e58ea3d15c2da66bce014898281fe237f2e0c2396f96c84c9e79.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ef/eff037b96b6a42120fdfa112a98d1e0749cdd56bd89acd647db448b08d7323ad.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-1<y<0\\,}.\n$$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186278573 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186278573 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186278580 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4y>{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\nII. $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\nIII. $∂A⊂A$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186278580 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4y>{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- $∂A⊂A$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186281306 1071 "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186281306 1071 "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186281306 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2\\}.\n$$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186281306 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2}.\n$$" 13194139534891 17592186045417 false] [17592186442850 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442851 13194139534891 17592186045417 true] [17592186442850 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442852 13194139534891 1759218604